  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for innovation in climate adaptation and resilience building solutions: Promoting climate adaptation and resilience through innovation and entrepreneurship for green jobs in Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the PARS Child Project in Angola is to reduce climate vulnerability and enhance resilience of vulnerable communities in southern and coastal provinces # particularly Cunene, Namibe, Hu&#xed;la, Cuando Cubango, Luanda, and Benguela # to climate change. This will be achieved through the private sector by creating an enabling environment, promoting innovation, facilitating technology transfer, and deploying innovative adaptation and resilience-building solutions. The project places a specific focus on creating employment opportunities through Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in the water, energy, food and agriculture (WEFA) sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
